// Package conecta 是一个类型无关的通用对象池管理器，可包装任意对象（如连接、客户端句柄）并管理其生命周期：后台健康检查、按需创建与清理，支持按对象最大存活时间（可叠加随机抖动）主动淘汰到期对象，并提供阻塞式获取 GetWithContext——maxSize 封顶在途对象总数（已借出 + 池内空闲 + 在途创建预留，对齐 pgxpool.MaxConns / database/sql.MaxOpenConns）：在途对象全部借出后挂起等待归还、绝不突破创建，按 FIFO 公平唤醒，传播 context 的超时与取消（超时返回 context.DeadlineExceeded，取消返回 context.Canceled）。经 GetWithContext 取得的对象必须由调用方 Put 归还（或经池的销毁路径销毁），否则其在途配额永久泄漏、后续获取将无限期挂起。注意 GetOrCreate 的按需创建不受 maxSize 约束、在途对象总数可能瞬时超限（突破对象同样计入在途，突破期间 GetWithContext 挂起等待）。借出/归还路径提供决策钩子 BeforeGet/AfterPut（区别于纯观察者的 Callback，钩子返回值改变流程：拒绝即销毁该对象并释放在途配额；AfterPut 的拒绝错误由 Put 原样透传）与 TestOnBorrow 便捷预设（未设 BeforeGet 时以 pingFunc 校验每次借出）；钩子在所有池内锁之外调用，panic 被 recover 转为携带 panic 值的 error，钩子自身缺陷不拖垮池；钩子内禁止重入池的写操作 API。创建路径与 Put 对称拒绝 nil 值：newFunc 成功必须返回非 nil 元素，(nil, nil) 一律返回 ErrValueIsNil，绝不静默计数。水位管理：MinIdle 维持最小空闲水位——后台扫描发现有效空闲不足时在扫描末尾异步补齐（独立 goroutine、CAS 标志节流防创建风暴、经 reserveSlot 走在途封顶、创建失败即停止本轮依赖下个扫描周期重试、尊重 ctx 取消零泄漏；补齐属池内部创建，不触发 BeforeGet/AfterPut 钩子。注意：启用 MinIdle 后 NewFunc 加入后台回调警告清单——补齐 goroutine 中 NewFunc panic 将终止进程（后台 goroutine 的 panic 调用方中间件 recover 不可达）、慢或挂起的 NewFunc 会延迟 Stop；standalone Cleanup 后池仍存活，下一轮扫描会把水位自动补回 MinIdle），MaxIdleTime 回收持续空闲超时的对象（销毁路径与 ping/lifetime 完全同构，tombstone 留队列占容量直至 Get 或下一轮扫描末尾的 tombstone GC 回收——GC 每轮把队列占用收敛回真实活对象数，零流量空闲池的 size 亦有界），且回收尊重 MinIdle 下限绝不打穿保温水位（对齐 HikariCP idleTimeout 仅在 idle > minimumIdle 时生效的语义）；两者与 MaxLifetime 无冲突可同设——MaxLifetime 是年龄硬上限，MaxIdleTime 是空闲软回收（自最近一次入队起算，借出并归还即重置空闲计时）。可观测性：Stats() 返回纯数据快照——瞬时水位（ActiveCount/IdleCount/TombstoneCount 与 MaxSize/MinIdle 回显）、累计计数（TotalCreated/TotalDestroyed/TotalBorrowed/TotalReturned）、五分类销毁原因（DestroyedByPing/ByLifetime/ByIdle/ByBorrow/ByStop，恒等式 TotalDestroyed == 五分类之和由单一计数入口在结构上保证）与拒绝/等待指标（EmptyCount/FullPutCount/WaitCount/WaitTimeoutCount/TotalWaitDuration），用户自行接入 Prometheus 等指标系统，主模块不引入监控依赖。已知边界（详见 README）：① Put 被 ErrPoolFull 拒绝时所有权不转移，对象与其在途配额均由调用方处置——未启用 MinIdle 的纯 Get/GetWithContext/Put 负载下该拒绝不可达；启用 MinIdle 后，轮换的 tombstone 窗口叠加补齐可使队列占用瞬时超限（tombstone GC 把窗口约束在约一个扫描周期内、在途封顶把峰值约束在 maxSize+minIdle），拒绝降级为瞬时可自愈：重试 Put 约一个扫描周期内成功（有测试钉住），永久搁浅需要 GetOrCreate 突破或外部对象填满队列参与；被拒后建议重试 Put 而非丢弃（丢弃 = 永久损失该格在途配额，自行 closeFunc 不触发池的配额释放；纯有界负载建议不混用 GetOrCreate；合法的显式丢弃出口 Discard API 为未来演进项）；② 外部对象（非池 newFunc 创建）经 Put 收编后被池销毁会消耗在途配额计数，封顶可瞬时虚增——属 Put(data any) 无来源信息的固有边界（releaseSlot 以 0 为下限防负漂移）；③ 定向唤醒的 FIFO 公平在“持续直接 Get 抢占归还对象”的对抗性负载下存在理论尾饥饿概率（-count=100 实证未现；强公平需归还直接移交变体，未实现）。主模块零外部依赖，队列实现可插拔。
// Package conecta is a type-agnostic generic object pool manager that wraps arbitrary objects (such as connections and client handles) and manages their lifecycle: background health checking, on-demand creation and cleanup, plus proactive eviction of objects that exceed their maximum lifetime (optionally spread by a random jitter). It also provides blocking acquisition via GetWithContext — maxSize caps the total in-flight object count (borrowed + idle in the pool + in-flight creation reservations, aligning with pgxpool.MaxConns / database/sql.MaxOpenConns): once every in-flight object is borrowed, callers suspend and wait for a return instead of ever creating beyond the cap, woken fairly in FIFO order, propagating context timeout and cancellation (a timeout returns context.DeadlineExceeded, a cancellation returns context.Canceled). An object obtained via GetWithContext must be returned by the caller via Put (or destroyed through a pool path); otherwise its in-flight slot leaks permanently and later acquisitions suspend indefinitely. Note that GetOrCreate's on-demand creation is NOT constrained by maxSize and the number of live objects may momentarily exceed the cap (break-through objects still count as in-flight, so GetWithContext suspends while the break-through persists). The borrow/return paths offer the decision hooks BeforeGet/AfterPut (as opposed to the pure-observer Callback, a hook's return value changes the flow: a rejection destroys that object and releases its in-flight slot; AfterPut's rejection error is passed through by Put as-is) plus the TestOnBorrow convenience preset (with no BeforeGet set, every borrow is validated via pingFunc); hooks are invoked outside every pool lock, panics are recovered into errors carrying the panic value so a buggy hook never takes the pool down, and re-entering the pool's mutating APIs from a hook is forbidden. The creation paths reject nil symmetrically with Put: a successful newFunc must return a non-nil element, and (nil, nil) uniformly returns ErrValueIsNil instead of being counted silently. Water-level management: MinIdle keeps a minimum idle water level — when the background scan finds the effective idle count below it, an async refill runs at the end of the pass (a dedicated goroutine, throttled by a CAS flag against creation storms, bounded by reserveSlot's in-flight cap, stopping the round on a creation failure so the next scan interval retries naturally, and honoring ctx cancellation with zero leaks; a refill is an internal creation and never fires the BeforeGet/AfterPut hooks. Note: with MinIdle enabled NewFunc joins the background-callback warning list — a NewFunc panic inside the refill goroutine terminates the process (no caller-side middleware recover can reach a background goroutine) and a slow or hanging NewFunc delays Stop; after a standalone Cleanup the pool stays alive and the next scan refills the water level back to MinIdle), while MaxIdleTime reclaims objects idling continuously beyond the duration (the destruction path is fully isomorphic to the ping/lifetime destructions, the tombstone staying in the queue occupying capacity until a Get — or the tombstone GC at the end of the next scan — reclaims it; the GC converges the queue occupancy back to the true live-object count every pass, keeping size bounded even on a zero-traffic idle pool) and the reclaim respects the MinIdle floor, never breaking the kept-warm water level (aligning with HikariCP's idleTimeout, which only applies when idle > minimumIdle); both compose with MaxLifetime without conflict — MaxLifetime is the hard age cap while MaxIdleTime is the soft idle reclaim (measured from the most recent enqueue; a borrow-and-return cycle restarts the idle clock). Observability: Stats() returns a pure-data snapshot — instantaneous water levels (ActiveCount/IdleCount/TombstoneCount plus the MaxSize/MinIdle echo), cumulative counters (TotalCreated/TotalDestroyed/TotalBorrowed/TotalReturned), the five destruction categories (DestroyedByPing/ByLifetime/ByIdle/ByBorrow/ByStop, with the identity TotalDestroyed == the sum of the five structurally guaranteed by the single counting entry point) and the rejection/wait metrics (EmptyCount/FullPutCount/WaitCount/WaitTimeoutCount/TotalWaitDuration), leaving users to wire it into Prometheus or any metrics system with no monitoring dependency in the main module. Known boundaries (see the README for details): ① a Put rejected with ErrPoolFull transfers no ownership — the value and its in-flight slot both stay the caller's to dispose of; the rejection is unreachable on a pure Get/GetWithContext/Put workload without MinIdle; with MinIdle enabled a rotation's tombstone window stacked with the refill top-up can transiently overflow the queue-occupancy counter (the tombstone GC bounds the window to ~one scan interval and the in-flight cap bounds the peak at maxSize+minIdle), degrading the rejection to transient and self-healing: a retried Put succeeds within ~one scan interval (pinned by a test), while permanent stranding requires GetOrCreate break-throughs or foreign objects filling the queue — retrying the Put is recommended over discarding (discarding = losing that in-flight slot permanently, and closing the value yourself never triggers the pool's quota release; prefer not to mix GetOrCreate into an otherwise pure bounded workload; an explicit legitimate Discard API is a future evolution item); ② a foreign object (not created by the pool's newFunc) adopted via Put consumes in-flight quota when the pool destroys it, so the cap may be transiently inflated — an inherent boundary of the provenance-free Put(data any) (releaseSlot floors at zero against negative drift); ③ the targeted FIFO wake is theoretically subject to tail starvation under an adversarial load of continuous direct Gets barging on returned objects (never observed in -count=100 runs; strong fairness would require a direct-handover return variant, not implemented). The main module has zero external dependencies and supports pluggable queue implementations.
package conecta
